From 23df536b670f502783ef6afd9d0fec4a5b564fe7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:16:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(pi): A/B GPT layout for systemd-sysupdate

The Pi 5 / CM5 images are a single MBR root, so they cannot update
themselves. systemd-sysupdate only writes partitions on a GPT disk
("Disk %s has no GPT disk label, not suitable."), and the Pi 5 bootloader
reads GPT (rpi-eeprom 2712 release notes, 2024-10-10 and 2025-01-22).

MARATHON_IMAGE_LAYOUT=ab now builds raspberry-pi5 as the A/B layout the
Raspberry Pi autoboot.txt documentation describes: partition 1 holds only
autoboot.txt, partitions 2 and 3 are FAT boot slots, 4 and 5 are ext4
root slots, and 6 is a data partition shared by both. Slot B is created
empty here, labelled _empty, so sysupdate writes the first update into it.
Each slot's partition label carries its IMAGE_VERSION, which is how
sysupdate and the boot slot's cmdline find it.

The GPT is kept, and each FAT32 partition gets its real start in the BPB's
hidden sectors, as 0032 does on the MBR layout.
---
 .gitignore                          |  3 +++
 mkosi.repart.ab-pi/00-autoboot.conf |  7 +++++++
 mkosi.repart.ab-pi/10-boot-a.conf   |  8 ++++++++
 mkosi.repart.ab-pi/11-boot-b.conf   |  5 +++++
 mkosi.repart.ab-pi/20-root-a.conf   |  8 ++++++++
 mkosi.repart.ab-pi/21-root-b.conf   |  5 +++++
 mkosi.repart.ab-pi/30-data.conf     |  6 ++++++
 scripts/build-image.py              | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 scripts/mkosi-configure.py          | 12 ++++++++----
 9 files changed, 75 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 mkosi.repart.ab-pi/00-autoboot.conf
 create mode 100644 mkosi.repart.ab-pi/10-boot-a.conf
 create mode 100644 mkosi.repart.ab-pi/11-boot-b.conf
 create mode 100644 mkosi.repart.ab-pi/20-root-a.conf
 create mode 100644 mkosi.repart.ab-pi/21-root-b.conf
